#: ../hacks/config/apple2.xml.h:16
msgid ""
"\n"
"An Apple ][+ computer simulation, in all its 1979 glory.  It also\n"
"reproduces the appearance of display on a color television set of the\n"
"period.\n"
"\n"
"In \"Basic Programming Mode\", a simulated user types in a BASIC program\n"
"and runs it.  In \"Text Mode\", it displays the output of a program, or\n"
"the contents of a file or URL.  In \"Slideshow Mode\", it chooses random\n"
"images and displays them within the limitations of the Apple ][\n"
"display hardware.  (Six available colors in hi-res mode!)\n"
"\n"
"On MacOS and Linux, this program is also a fully-functional VT100\n"
"emulator!  Run it as an application instead of as a screen saver and\n"
"you can use it as a terminal.\n"
"\n"
"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apple_II_series\n"
"\n"
"Written by Trevor Blackwell and Jamie Zawinski; 2003.\n"
"  "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"En Apple ][+ computersimulering, i al sin 1979 herlighed.  Det også\n"
"gengiver udseendet af displayet på et farvefjernsyn\n"
"periode.\n"
"\n"
"indholdet af en fil eller URL.  I \"Slideshow Mode\" vælger den tilfældigt\n"
"I \"Basic Programming Mode\" indtaster en simuleret bruger et BASIC-program\n"
"billeder og viser dem inden for Apples begrænsninger ][\n"
"og kører den.  display hardware.  I \"Tekst-tilstand\" viser den output fra "
"et program, eller\n"
"(Seks tilgængelige farver i højopløsningstilstand!)\n"
"\n"
"På MacOS og Linux er dette program også en fuldt funktionel VT100\n"
"emulator!  Kør det som et program i stedet for som en pauseskærm og\n"
"du kan bruge den som en terminal.\n"
"\n"
"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apple_II_series\n"
"\n"
"Skrevet af Trevor Blackwell og Jamie Zawinski; 2003.\n"
"  "

